---
source: crates/rumps-query/tests/scripts.rs
description: "; Test: Unit type and Option values\n; Tests blocks returning Unit, single-arm IF returning Unit, and Option behavior\n\n; === Block without tail returns Unit ===\n\nLET result = {\n  OUTPUT \"Side effect only\"\n}\nOUTPUT result\n; Expected: ()\n\nLET result2 = {\n  LET x = 42\n  OUTPUT x\n  ; No tail expression\n}\nOUTPUT result2\n; Expected: ()\n\n; === Block with tail returns value ===\n\nLET result3 = {\n  LET x = 42\n  x\n}\nOUTPUT result3\n; Expected: 42\n\n; === Single-arm IF returns Unit ===\n\n; Single-arm IF with false condition (body not evaluated)\nLET cond1 = IF FALSE {\n  OUTPUT \"never reached\"\n}\nOUTPUT cond1\n; Expected: ()\n\n; Single-arm IF with true condition (body evaluated, must be Unit)\nLET cond2 = IF TRUE {\n  OUTPUT \"side effect\"\n}\nOUTPUT cond2\n; Expected: ()\n\n; === Option values ===\n\n; Option.None\nOUTPUT Option.None\n; Expected: Option.None\n\n; Option.Some unwrapping with coalesce\nOUTPUT Option.Some(42) ?? 0\n; Expected: 42\n\n; Option.None fallback with coalesce\nOUTPUT Option.None ?? \"fallback\"\n; Expected: fallback\n\nOUTPUT \"Unit and Option test complete\"\n"
---
